      "writtenOn": "2026-05-31T19:25:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like the host doesn\u0027t really use the PERFFRZSTS registers? So perhaps we don\u0027t really need to support them (and thus, in particular, don\u0027t need to add the DMAR_PERFFRZOFF_REG definition to iommu.h, and so on)?",
      "revId": "bc0e9123504f91f63878def0e58be942cb8e7d45",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "55e4c5e1_2afa178f",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/pkvm/iommu_pmu.c",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 233,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-31T19:25:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess the reason why we only support the first PERFOVFSTS register is that the host currently uses no more than 64 counters (IOMMU_PMU_IDX_MAX), so they all fit in one register? But it is not so obvious, so may be worth adding a short comment about it?",
      "revId": "bc0e9123504f91f63878def0e58be942cb8e7d45",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
