        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-31T19:25:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`num_ctrl` is capped at IOMMU_PMU_IDX_MAX in `iommu_pmu_num_counters()`, so we never have the `num_cntr \u003e BITS_PER_TYPE(u64)` case (otherwise we would need to support multiple PERFOVFSTS registers, per above)? So `GENMASK_ULL(num_cntr - 1, 0)` covers all needed cases?\n\n...Besides, using `BITS_PER_TYPE(u64)` instead of just 64 surely is an overkill? :)",
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "efe158c3_234aa015",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "drivers/iommu/intel/pkvm/iommu_pmu.c",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 239,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 241,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "\t\tinfo-\u003ewritable_mask \u003d GENMASK_ULL(num_cntr - 1, 0);\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "revId": "bc0e9123504f91f63878def0e58be942cb8e7d45",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1f76a75e_a9258c87",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/pkvm/iommu_pmu.c",
