      "lineNbr": 239,
      "author": {
        "id": 3702829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-01T10:31:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e num_ctrl is capped at IOMMU_PMU_IDX_MAX in iommu_pmu_num_counters(), so we never have the num_cntr \u003e BITS_PER_TYPE(u64) case (otherwise we would need to support multiple PERFOVFSTS registers, per above)? So GENMASK_ULL(num_cntr - 1, 0) covers all needed cases?\n\nAgreed.\n\n\u003e ...Besides, using BITS_PER_TYPE(u64) instead of just 64 surely is an overkill? :)\n\nSorry about this, I did not intend to over-engineer. BITS_PER_TYPE is compile time and doesn\u0027t incur runtime cost and my intention was to have implicitly commented code (better readability than 64). I have removed it now.",
      "parentUuid": "fdebe2cf_f20ea566",
      "revId": "bc0e9123504f91f63878def0e58be942cb8e7d45",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
